course: dictionary
lesson: 9589
title: Streetlights and context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A streetlight is a tall lamp on a pole beside a road that lights up the street at night. You can work out this meaning from the words around it, even if you have never thought about the word before.
explain: «Council tax goes to the local council for shared things like bins, streetlights and libraries.» Bins, libraries and roads are things a whole town shares, so a streetlight must be a shared light that the council looks after along the street.
explain: «Robins ... can even sing at night under streetlights.» Under a streetlight means right beneath the lamp on its pole. Check by swapping in your meaning: "sing at night under a tall lamp beside the road" still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: A streetlight is a tall lamp on a pole beside a road.
fact: Streetlights light up the street at night, so people can see and be seen when walking.
fact: Streetlights use electricity, and many now use LED bulbs.
fact: Children are often told to be home «when the streetlights come on».
fact: The local council pays for shared things such as streetlights, bins, roads and libraries.
exercise: «Council tax goes to the local council for shared things like bins, streetlights and libraries.» What is a streetlight? | A bus stop with a bench | A small shop at the end of a road | A bin on wheels that the bin men empty | *A tall lamp on a pole beside a road that lights up the street at night
exercise: «Robins can even sing at night under streetlights.» Where would a robin be singing? | *Under a lamp on a pole beside a road | Deep under the sea in a cave | Inside a rubbish bin | Up on the moon
exercise: Children are told to be home «when the streetlights come on». What does this tell you? | It is raining very hard | *It is getting dark, so it is time to go home | The shops are just opening | It is early morning and school is starting
test: What do streetlights use to give out light? | Wood from the trees | Sunshine | Water from the river | *Electricity, often through LED bulbs
test: Which of these best describes what streetlights do? | Keep robins away from gardens | Grow flowers along the road | *Help people see and be seen when walking at night | Make the rain stop
exam: A child asks, «What is a streetlight?» Which answer is right? | *A tall lamp on a pole beside a road that lights up the street at night | A shop that sells lamps | A kind of bin for rubbish | A plant that grows beside the street
